## Import Knowledge Store documents from a Unity Catalog Volume

Context:
The Knowledge Store only accepted local uploads, so documents already stored
in a UC Volume had to be downloaded to a laptop and uploaded again. Users can
now paste a `/Volumes/...` file or folder path, or browse catalog → schema →
volume → folder and multi-select files. Files are listed and read with the
caller's own token (OBO, fail-closed in App mode), never the app service
principal, and then enter exactly the same parse-once pipeline as an upload.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/document/VolumeDocumentSource.py (new)
   - Validates paths (`/Volumes/<catalog>/<schema>/<volume>[/...]`, no `..`,
     `.`, empty segments, backslashes or control characters, max 1024 chars).
   - Plans imports: a file path is checked by HEAD; a folder contributes its
     supported direct children only (not recursive); max 50 paths and 50 files
     per request; duplicate paths dropped; a second file with an already-used
     name is reported instead of overwriting the first.
   - Type and the 10 MB cap are checked from metadata before download; the
     download is streamed and aborted past the cap (defence in depth).
   - Maps 401/403/404/other Files API statuses to `AuthorizationError` (with a
     `files.files` scope hint), `NotFoundError` and `InfrastructureError`.
   - `browse()` lists one folder with `supported` / `too_large` flags.
2. src/back/core/databricks/document/VolumeDocument.py (new)
   - Frozen record for one planned volume file (path, filename, size, error).
3. src/back/core/databricks/uc/VolumeFileService.py
   - `head_file`, `list_directory_page` (follows `next_page_token` up to a cap)
     and `read_binary_file_capped` (streamed, stops reading past the cap).
4. src/back/core/databricks/__init__.py, src/back/core/databricks/document/__init__.py
   - Re-export `VolumeDocument` and `VolumeDocumentSource`.
5. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   - Extract Method: `_submit_document` (size cap → `prepare_upload` →
     background parse → result row) and `_document_batch_response`, shared by
     upload and volume import; `upload_documents` drops below the 100-line
     budget.
   - New `GET /domain/documents/volume/browse` and
     `POST /domain/documents/import-volume`; `_make_volume_document_source`
     binds the Files API client through `get_data_plane_client` (user token in
     App mode, 403 when it is missing). Results carry `source_path`; the
     registry-save rule and the existing status/viewer gates on
     `/domain/documents/` POSTs apply unchanged.
6. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_documents.html
   - "Import from Unity Catalog Volume" section in the upload card: path input,
     Browse panel with catalog / schema / volume pickers, folder list, Import
     selected / Import this folder.
7. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-documents-volume.js (new), src/front/templates/domain.html
   - `VolumeImport`: reuses `/settings/catalogs|schemas|volumes` for pickers,
     browses folders via the new endpoint, posts `{paths}` (CSRF header via the
     global fetch wrapper), refreshes the shared document list. Paths travel
     in data attributes with delegated handlers (no inline JS); names are
     escaped and marked `data-i18n-skip`. Respects `window.isActiveVersion`.
8. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css, src/front/static/global/css/config.css
   - `#docVolumeImport` is disabled exactly where `#docDropZone` is
     (read-only version, Viewer, locked); scroll cap for the folder list.
9. src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js, tests/units/front/i18n_untranslated_baseline.json
   - Korean strings for the new UI; the path placeholder is a baseline token.
10. databricks.yml
    - UI app `user_api_scopes` gains `files.files` (Files API on behalf of the
      user). Users re-consent once after deploy.
11. docs/user-guide.md, docs/deployment.md, docs/architecture.md
    - Import workflow, rules table, scope/consent note, architecture notes.
12. Tests
    - tests/units/core/test_volume_document_source.py (new): path validation,
      size limit (metadata and stream), unsupported types, folder listing and
      cap, duplicates, status mapping.
    - tests/units/core/test_volume_file_service.py: new Files API methods and
      the user token as bearer in App mode with SP credentials present.
    - tests/units/api/test_document_volume_import_routes.py (new): routes with
      a mocked Files API through the real data-plane client; user token on
      every call, fail-closed without a token, shared pipeline, gating.
    - tests/units/front/test_domain_documents_ui.py,
      tests/units/front/test_domain_documents_volume_behaviour.py (new):
      markup/gating contracts and node-executed behaviour (payload, read-only
      gate, navigation, HTML escaping).
    - tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py: `files.files` scope.
    - tests/units/architecture/baseline.json: drop the `upload_documents`
      size-budget entry (now within budget).

Notes:
- `domain_documents` has no column for the source path; adding one needs a
  schema migration, so the path is returned in the import response and logged
  instead of being persisted.
- The existing `UCFileDialog` was not reused: it is single-select, requires a
  warehouse pick that saves settings, reads through `/read-volume-file` with
  the app identity, and its `/browse-volume` calls a missing
  `list_volume_files` method.
- Catalog / schema / volume *names* come from the existing `/settings/*`
  listing APIs (app identity, as elsewhere in the app); folder contents and
  file bytes are always read as the user.

