## Pin English as the default UI language

Context:
Among the registered UI languages (English, Korean), English must be the
default whenever the user has not picked one. The resolution order was
already cookie `ob_lang` -> deploy default `ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG` -> `en` on
the server, and cookie -> `<html lang>` -> `en` on the client, with no
browser-locale detection. Korean showed up only where a deploy config set
`APP_UI_LANG=ko`. This change locks that contract with tests (a Korean
browser locale alone must not switch the UI to Korean; an explicit choice in
the language selector always wins) and documents it. No behaviour change.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
   - Docstring on `resolveLang()` stating the order and that
     `navigator.language` is deliberately ignored.
   - `resolveLang` exposed on `window.OB_I18N_CORE` so unit tests can run it.
2. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   - `resolve_ui_lang()` docstring: `Accept-Language` is deliberately not
     consulted.
3. tests/units/front/test_i18n.py
   - Rendered page: `Accept-Language: ko-KR` with no cookie -> `<html lang="en">`
     and no Korean dictionary; `ob_lang=en` overrides a Korean deploy default.
   - Client resolution (node harness with a Korean `navigator` stub): no
     stored choice -> en, stored ko -> ko, stored en -> en (also over a
     Korean `<html lang>`), unsupported stored value -> en, Korean browser
     locale alone -> en.
4. docs/user-guide.md, docs/deployment.md
   - Note that the browser's language setting is not used.

